# process.argv is made by the host at its first read and kept; nobody in this program replaces it. The read was declared to run unknown code and stood in every turn.
# It bears what its row of the table says (the heap, a throw, no code of the program). Under no handler it counts as a read of what is seen: it stands in front of a loop whose every turn asks for it and whose turns run no other code and write nothing, and the length of the list behind it.
# Where only some turns ask, it stays in the turn: the host is not made to build what may never be read.
# f1 = counted, f2 = inSomeTurns
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = GetBuiltinValue builtin=ProcessArgv
# CHECK-NOT: mayCallUnknownCode
# CHECK: = GetArrayLength
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: = GetBuiltinValue
# CHECK-NOT: = GetArrayLength
# CHECK: Return
# RUN(SOME): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
